  «text (5140,897) 0.8 5 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿Notes:\n* SIMCLK is NOT an actual device pin...\n* This device contains an internal oscillator.\n   However, that is not used for emulation.\n   Instead, SIMCLK is used to sychronize the\n   micro-controller to the QSpice simulation.\n   Each falling edge of SIMCLK steps the device\n   by 1 instruction cycle. \n* Set OscFreq to match device oscillator \n   frequency as defined in the *.hex/*.elf\n   configuration bits/fuses."»
  «text (-2530,2022) 1.6 5 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿ATmega32 Test Fixture"»
  «text (750,-1391) 1 5 0 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿.param OscFreq=8Meg\n.param CyclesPerInst=1\n.param InstHz=OscFreq/CyclesPerInst"»
  «text (700,-1250) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿Device Clock Parameters (check these against MCU code)"»
  «text (3201,889) 1.25 14 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿"Charlieplexed" LEDs"»
  «text (5350,-1250) 1 7 0 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿.tran 625Âµ"»
  «text (5350,-2100) 1 7 0 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿.plot I(D1)\n.plot I(D2)\n.plot I(D3)\n.plot I(D4)\n.plot I(D5)\n.plot I(D6)"»
  «text (-2510,1647) 1 5 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿The most current schematics, code, and documentation are available in the QMdbSim2 project folder at https://github.com/robdunn4/QSpice."»
  «text (650,-2450) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿Note:  XTAL pins unused -- timing is driven by SIMCLK.\nJust makng QSpice netlist happy..."»
  «text (2450,-4109) 1.25 5 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿Note:  The Microchip simulator does not support the AC\n(analog comparator) and ADC functions of this device."»
